baidunetdisk-rs for Debian
----------------------------

The build uses the cargo debhelper build system. Upstream depends on the
kasumi GUI framework through path dependencies inside the original workspace:

    kasumi        = { path = "../kasumi/crates/kasumi" }
    kasumi-core   = { path = "../kasumi/crates/kasumi-core" }
    kasumi-backend= { path = "../kasumi/crates/kasumi-backend" }

 1. Vendor the dependency closure:

        cd kasumi && cargo vendor vendor/ > ../baidunetdisk-rs/.cargo/config.toml

    (or ship the kasumi crates themselves as separate source packages, e.g.
    librust-kasumi-dev and librust-kasumi-backend-dev).

 2. Generate the orig tarball from the source tree and unpack it into this
    directory as ../baidunetdisk-rs_<version>.orig.tar.xz.

 3. Build:

        dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

The resulting binary package is baidunetdisk-rs_<version>_<arch>.deb. The
upstream asset directory (SVG icons) is resolved relative to the executable
(/usr/lib/baidunetdisk-rs/assets), or with the BAIDUNETDISK_ASSETS environment
variable, and otherwise falls back to the build-time source path.
